{title: And the Walls Came Down}
{subtitle: Joshua 6:1–5; 6:15–20}
{key: C}
{tempo: 120}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [–] |
| [C] | ×10
| [F] | [F] | [Am] | [G] |
| [C] | [C] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Joshua marched around the town
[F]And the walls came [C]down
Seven priests with trumpets sound
[G]And the walls came [C]down
Six days round and nobody spoke
[F]And the walls came [C]down
On the seventh day the people shout
[G]And the walls came [C]down
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Shout, shout, the Lord has [F]given you the [C]city
Blow the trumpet, [G]raise the [C]cry
Shout, shout, the Lord has [F]given you the [C]city
Jericho is [G]falling [C]down
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Seven times on the seventh day
[F]And the walls came [C]down
Trumpets blew and the people prayed
[G]And the walls came [C]down
A great shout went up to the sky
[F]And the walls came [C]down
Every stone fell where it lay
[G]And the walls came [C]down
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Shout, shout, the Lord has [F]given you the [C]city
Blow the trumpet, [G]raise the [C]cry
Shout, shout, the Lord [F]has given you [C]the city
Jericho is [G]falling [C]down
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Outro}
